 *    (prompt, thread linkage, config fields)
 * 3. Attempt to access a non-existent poll ID (expect error)
 * 4. If supported, attempt to access a poll a member is not authorized to see (if
 *    business logic distinguishes access)
 *
 * Steps:
 *
 * - Use the API to create at least one poll. Store the ID(s).
 * - Use the poll detail endpoint to fetch the poll by ID. Verify all actual
 *   fields match what was submitted/created.
 * - Attempt to retrieve a poll by a random (non-existent) UUID. Expect 404 error.
 * - (If supported) Attempt to retrieve a poll owned by another member or
 *   inaccessible per business rule. Expect Forbidden/404 error. (If there are
 *   no such rules, skip this step)
 */
export async function test_api_prefix_member_polls_test_view_poll_details_as_member_success_and_error_cases(
