 * This test ensures that the system correctly enforces the requirement for all
 * necessary fields in a PUT (overwrite) update scenario. According to schema
 * and RESTful convention, missing required fields in a PUT payload should
 * result in a validation error.
 *
 * Steps:
 *
 * 1. Create an initial valid incident report as an admin.
 * 2. Attempt to update the report with an incomplete payload (omit one or more
 *    schema-required fields).
 * 3. Assert that the update operation fails due to validation error (runtime error
 *    is thrown).
 *
 * Notes:
 *
 * - The IDiscussionboardIncidentReport.IUpdate type defines required fields
 *   (incident_code, status, description, updated_at). At least one of these
 *   will be omitted in the update request.
 * - TypeScript will not allow constructing an invalid IUpdate object, so to
 *   simulate the scenario, this test uses an explicit 'as unknown as
 *   IDiscussionboardIncidentReport.IUpdate' with a partial object to force the
 *   runtime error. In production, this is not recommended, but is necessary for
 *   e2e validation of server-side required-ness.
 */
export async function test_api_prefix_admin_policyAudit_incidentReports_test_partial_update_incident_report_missing_required_fields(
