 * 3. As moderator, fetch the post edit log detail using the valid id, and assert
 *    all fields and schema compliance.
 * 4. As moderator, fetch with a non-existent id and expect error (404).
 * 5. Attempt to fetch the edit log as guest (no auth) and as member (normal
 *    connection); both should return an error (forbidden/unauthorized).
 */
export async function test_api_moderator_test_get_post_edit_log_detail_moderator_with_valid_and_invalid_id(
